The original constructor default-constructs `values` and `stringIndexes` and then copy-assigns into them. Copying them in the member initializer list builds each one directly from the source in a single step, avoiding the separate construction and assignment.

Any other members are still default-initialized, as before, so observable behavior is unchanged.

```cpp
FieldBase::FieldBase(const FieldBase &field)
    : values(field.values),
      stringIndexes(field.stringIndexes)
{
}
```